From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm630: install uplink filters from AP

The downstream SDM660 DT says that modem firmware owns the embedded pipe
filter table.  That contract is not fulfilled by the firmware/mainline
combination used on lavender.  After QMI supplied 24 filters, an IPv4
status from pipe 4 reported filter rule 0xff, no route match, and delivery
to the default exception pipe 2.

Do not advertise modem-owned embedded filters for ipa2-lite.  The driver
has the decoded QMI rules and the downstream hardware-rule encoder, so it
can install the IPv4/IPv6 tables for APPS_LAN_WAN_PROD and send the
FILTER_INSTALLED notification to the modem.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
index 860a9ce0e..8939bb30f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
@@ -1053,7 +1053,6 @@ ipa: ipa@14780000 {
 			iommus = <&anoc2_smmu 0x19C0>;
 			modem-remoteproc = <&remoteproc_mss>;
-			qcom,modem-cfg-emb-pipe-flt;
 			status = "okay";
 
 			ipa_smmu_uc: ipa-smmu-uc {
